sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design, container runtime (ADR 0250 step 6, docs/reference/development-containers.md#destroy): `instance:destroy` of a container Instance. The kind and its step names follow docs/cli/instance/destroy.mmd; the intent carries `runtime: container`.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:destroy
  %% kind: instance.destroy
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane C icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant C as Container<br/>via incus exec
  CLI->>GW: instance:destroy<br/>INSTANCE
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:destroy INSTANCE`
  %%> - syntax: `<instance> [--force]`
  Note over GW: Validate, mark removing<br/>no new pairings
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has node access to the Instance's Node; no other change runs on the Instance
  %%> - the Instance is not the source of an Instance that is still being created
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Instance is `removing`; the Conn layer refuses new pairings with its T3 server
  %%> - a task is recorded with the full intent
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-destroy
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  opt the container is stopped
    SW->>C: Start the container<br/>incus start
    %%> Why:
    %%> - the checks below read the workspace and T3; the Route is not published again
  end
  SW->>C: Check work and turns<br/>Ansible · tags check
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - as `agent`: unpushed commits and uncommitted files in the workspace, as for a checkout today
  %%> - asks T3's MCP endpoint for threads with a running or queued turn
  %%> Refuses:
  %%> - unpushed work, as today; a running turn with `instance.turn_running`
  %%> - `--force` skips both checks
  SW->>N: Revoke the pairings<br/>child conn-pairing-revoke
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - revokes every client session and unused link that Orbit paired on this T3 server
  SW->>N: Withdraw the Route<br/>child route-withdraw
  SW->>C: Stop Processes, teardown<br/>Ansible · tags teardown
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - stops the Processes, then runs the Project's teardown steps as `orbit`
  SW->>N: Delete the container<br/>incus delete --force
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - deletes the container with its T3 state and thread history, its proxy device and its firewall route rule
  %%> - the source container stays
  opt database on a Database server
    SW->>N: Drop owner and database<br/>child database-destroy
  end
  alt all steps pass
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    Note over GW: Remove Instance records<br/>T3 server removed
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the Instance, its runtime and its Route are removed; the T3 server's record is marked removed and its stored session deleted
    %%> - the port returns to `t3_ports`
  else a check refuses
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>instance.turn_running
    Note over GW: Back to active
    %%> Result:
    %%> - nothing was removed; the Instance is active again and pairing opens again
  else a later step fails
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step, error_code
    Note over GW: Keep removing
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again; it skips what is already gone
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
  end
